@page "/docs/extensions/icons"

<Seo Canonical="/docs/extensions/icons" Title="Blazorise Icons component" Description="Learn how to use Blazorise icon components and icon providers to represent actions, states, navigation, and commands with Font Awesome and other supported icon sets." />

<DocsPageTitle Path="Extensions/Icons">
    Blazorise Icons component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Icons are visual symbols that represent actions, states, or navigation options.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Blazorise ships with multiple icon providers and supports registering custom icon libraries.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    To use the <Code>Icon</Code> component, install one of the <Code>Blazorise.Icons.*</Code> packages first.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Installation
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Install an icon provider package from NuGet.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="NuGet">
        Install the package for the icon provider you want to use.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSourceGroup AriaLabel="Icon provider package">
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="IconsNugetInstallExample" CodeTitle="Font Awesome" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="AntDesignIconsNugetInstallExample" CodeTitle="AntDesign" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="BootstrapIconsNugetInstallExample" CodeTitle="Bootstrap" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="FluentUIIconsNugetInstallExample" CodeTitle="Fluent UI" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="MaterialIconsNugetInstallExample" CodeTitle="Material" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="LucideIconsNugetInstallExample" CodeTitle="Lucide" />
    </DocsPageSectionSourceGroup>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="CSS">
        Add the stylesheet for your icon provider inside the <Code Tag>head</Code> section of <Code>wwwroot/index.html</Code> for standalone WebAssembly, <Code>_Layout.cshtml</Code> or <Code>_Host.cshtml</Code> for Blazor Server, or <Code>Components/App.razor</Code> for a Blazor Web App.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSourceGroup AriaLabel="Icon provider stylesheets">
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="FontAwesomeCSSExample" CodeTitle="Font Awesome" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="AntDesignIconsCSSExample" CodeTitle="AntDesign" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="BootstrapIconsCSSExample" CodeTitle="Bootstrap">
            The Bootstrap Icons stylesheet is required for some custom icon styles to work.
        </DocsPageSectionSource>
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="FluentIconsCSSExample" CodeTitle="Fluent Font">
            Fluent icons use the CSS font by default and render at a default size of 20px.
        </DocsPageSectionSource>
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="FluentSvgIconsCSSExample" CodeTitle="Fluent SVG">
            Replace the Fluent font stylesheet with this SVG stylesheet and enable SVG rendering in the registration below. Icons render at a default size of 20px.
        </DocsPageSectionSource>
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="MaterialCSSExample" CodeTitle="Material">
            The Material icon stylesheet is required for some custom icon styles to work.
        </DocsPageSectionSource>
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="LucideIconsCSSExample" CodeTitle="Lucide" />
    </DocsPageSectionSourceGroup>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Registrations">
        Register the icon provider that matches the package and stylesheet you selected. Keep your existing Blazorise and CSS provider registration.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSourceGroup AriaLabel="Icon provider registration">
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="RegistrationsExample" CodeTitle="Font Awesome" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="AntDesignIconsRegistrationExample" CodeTitle="AntDesign" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="BootstrapIconsRegistrationExample" CodeTitle="Bootstrap" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="FluentUIIconsRegistrationExample" CodeTitle="Fluent Font" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="FluentSvgIconsRegistrationExample" CodeTitle="Fluent SVG">
            Enable SVG rendering when registering Fluent icons. Existing <Code>Icon</Code> component usage remains the same.
        </DocsPageSectionSource>
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="MaterialIconsRegistrationExample" CodeTitle="Material" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="LucideIconsRegistrationExample" CodeTitle="Lucide" />
    </DocsPageSectionSourceGroup>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Basic Example">
        The most basic example of using an icon is to use the <Code>Icon</Code> component. You can set the icon name using the <Code>IconName</Code> property.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="IconBasicExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <IconBasicExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Custom">
        You can also use a real icon name instead of predefined enum. Note that this is not the preferred way of using icons, but it can be useful in some cases.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Outlined FullWidth>
        <IconCustomExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
    <DocsPageSectionSourceGroup AriaLabel="Custom icon name">
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="IconCustomExample" CodeTitle="Font Awesome" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="AntDesignIconCustomExample" CodeTitle="AntDesign" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="BootstrapIconCustomExample" CodeTitle="Bootstrap" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="FluentUIIconCustomExample" CodeTitle="Fluent UI" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="MaterialIconCustomExample" CodeTitle="Material" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="LucideIconCustomExample" CodeTitle="Lucide" />
    </DocsPageSectionSourceGroup>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Icon Names">
        Preferred way to define icon is to use an enum <Code>IconName</Code>. That way every icon will be applied automatically based on the icon package that you're using.

        When the shared enum does not contain the icon you need, use a constant from your provider's icon-name class. Select your provider below to see its syntax.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Outlined FullWidth>
        <IconNamesExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
    <DocsPageSectionSourceGroup AriaLabel="Provider icon constants">
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="IconNamesExample" CodeTitle="Font Awesome" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="AntDesignIconNamesExample" CodeTitle="AntDesign" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="BootstrapIconNamesExample" CodeTitle="Bootstrap" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="FluentUIIconNamesExample" CodeTitle="Fluent UI" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="MaterialIconNamesExample" CodeTitle="Material" />
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="LucideIconNamesExample" CodeTitle="Lucide" />
    </DocsPageSectionSourceGroup>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Style">
        Blazorise exposes common icon styles through <Code>IconStyle</Code>. To change it you can use one of the supported styles:
        <UnorderedList>
            <UnorderedListItem>Solid</UnorderedListItem>
            <UnorderedListItem>Regular</UnorderedListItem>
            <UnorderedListItem>Light</UnorderedListItem>
            <UnorderedListItem>DuoTone</UnorderedListItem>
        </UnorderedList>

        Not all icon providers support all styles. If a style is not supported by the selected provider, it can fall back to the provider default or render the same base icon.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="IconStyleExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <IconStyleExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Style support">
        The table below compares how the built-in icon providers handle <Code>IconStyle</Code> values.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="IconSizeExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <Table>
            <TableHeader ThemeContrast="ThemeContrast.Light">
                <TableRow>
                    <TableHeaderCell>Provider</TableHeaderCell>
                    <TableHeaderCell>Solid</TableHeaderCell>
                    <TableHeaderCell>Regular</TableHeaderCell>
                    <TableHeaderCell>Light</TableHeaderCell>
                    <TableHeaderCell>DuoTone</TableHeaderCell>
                    <TableHeaderCell>Notes</TableHeaderCell>
                </TableRow>
            </TableHeader>
            <TableBody>
                <TableRow>
                    <TableRowCell>AntDesign</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Not supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Uses AntDesign icon themes.</TableRowCell>
                </TableRow>
                <TableRow>
                    <TableRowCell>Bootstrap Icons</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Single style only</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Not supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Not supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Not supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell><Code>IconStyle</Code> does not change the rendered icon.</TableRowCell>
                </TableRow>
                <TableRow>
                    <TableRowCell>Fluent UI</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Not supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Not supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Regular is the default; <Code>IconStyle.Solid</Code> selects the filled variant.</TableRowCell>
                </TableRow>
                <TableRow>
                    <TableRowCell>Font Awesome</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Requires matching Font Awesome assets</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Requires matching Font Awesome assets</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Support depends on the Font Awesome CSS and font files loaded by the app.</TableRowCell>
                </TableRow>
                <TableRow>
                    <TableRowCell>Material Icons</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Maps Blazorise styles to Material icon font families.</TableRowCell>
                </TableRow>
                <TableRow>
                    <TableRowCell>Lucide</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Single style only</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Single style only</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Not supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Not supported</TableRowCell>
                    <TableRowCell>Lucide is a single outline SVG icon set.</TableRowCell>
                </TableRow>
            </TableBody>
        </Table>
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Size">
        You can set the size to one of the supported below.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Outlined FullWidth>
        <IconSizeExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Global options">
        Defining styles on each icon can become very tedious with time. That's why we give you an option to specify them globally. This way, you will have consistent styling across the application, and you can still override them on the icon if you need to.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSource Code="IconGlobalSettingsExample" />
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageApi>
    <DocsPageApiItem Url="docs/extensions/icons/api" Name="<Icon />" />
</DocsPageApi>